The attached image illustrates the uptake of Nano-11 nanoparticles and ovalbumin (OVA) antigen by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) via confocal microscopy. The top row shows BMDCs phagocytizing AF647-labeled Nano-11 (red fluorescence). The middle row demonstrates minimal uptake of soluble FITC-labeled OVA (green fluorescence) by BMDCs. The bottom row highlights significantly enhanced OVA uptake and clear co-localization (yellow in the merged image) when OVA is adsorbed to Nano-11, indicating that Nano-11 effectively delivers antigens intracellularly to dendritic cells, which is crucial for initiating an immune response.